From a5209f484aa496d5b8da9df8a4cb86ad250ec4af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:59:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 239/241] trans: enumerate the dyn-method shims' receiver types
 with the others

skim 5.7.3 died in Trans Auto Impls:

    BUG: ASSERT FAIL: src/trans/auto_impls.cpp:1149:!params.has_types():
    Generic drop impl encountered during auto_impls (should have been populated during enum)

A `<dyn Trait as Trait>::method` used as a function value gets a shim in
Trans_AutoImpls, after enumeration. For `self: Box<Self>` the shim's
receiver local is `Box<()>`, which only reached the type list through
Trans_Enumerate_Types_Function at that point: nobody enumerated
`<Box<()> as Drop>::drop` (a generic impl), and the drop-glue pass has
no way to add it.

The unit-receiver type is a function of the method's receiver kind
(`&move ()`/`&()`, `Box<(), A>`, the custom receiver with `Self = ()`):
Trans_AutoImpls_DynMethodUnitReceiver computes it, the shim builder uses
it, and Trans_Enumerate_Types visits it for every trait_object_methods
entry, so its Drop impl is enumerated and monomorphised like any other.
The assertion names the type now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
